{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789758850,"nonce":"AOGUMQe/VzgfVOv4/iiYQk1Qwfw=","title":"Reading an undeclared field during inference typed it Object and widened the field for good","message":"Each inference round resets the classes to their declared layouts, so a function analysed before the constructor that declares a field saw the field missing; Typer read a missing field of a Class receiver as Object, the write back (a.x = a.x + a.vx) joined the field to Object, and Float never won it back. bench_nbody's Body had x, y, z, vx, vy, vz as DynamicBox fields: advance boxed every float operation (32 mallocs per call, 13 KB per call, 330 collections, 65 s against 0.7 s). Now a missing field reads as Unknown until Module.settled is set after the fixpoint (types.rs Typer attribute arm; lib.rs sets settled). Reproducer: class Body with three float fields, a = bodies[0]; a.x = a.x + a.vx; ZYNTAX_TRACE_TYPES=1 showed x: Object.","files":null}]}